[187.635692, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b7\u001b[2;77H\u001b[38;5;210m\u2584\u001b[38;5;210m\u2580\u001b[38;5;210m\u2588 \u001b[38;5;216m\u2588\u001b[38;5;216m\u2580\u001b[38;5;216m\u2584\u001b[38;5;216m\u2580\u001b[38;5;216m\u2588 \u001b[38;5;216m\u2580\u001b[38;5;222m\u2588\u001b[38;5;222m\u2580\u001b[0m\u001b[3;77H\u001b[38;5;210m\u2588\u001b[38;5;210m\u2580\u001b[38;5;210m\u2588 \u001b[38;5;216m\u2588 \u001b[38;5;216m\u2580 \u001b[38;5;216m\u2588 \u001b[38;5;222m\u2584\u001b[38;5;222m\u2588\u001b[38;5;222m\u2584\u001b[0m\u001b[4;77H\u001b]8;;https://www.superinference.org\u0007\u001b[2mwww.superinference.org\u001b[22m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b8\u001b[1;1H\u001b[J\u2022 \u001b[1mrefactored.py\u001b[22m \u2014 same interface and __main__ block, but the whole decision tree collapses into one\r\r\ndict.get(code, fallback). The fallback reconstructs the category from code // 100 using a small\r\r\nclass map, so unknown codes like 418 still resolve to 418 Client Error.\r\r\n\r\r\n\u2605 Insight \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\r\r\n- **Data over control flow:** nested conditionals encode a lookup table in branching logic; a dict\r\r\nmakes that table explicit, so adding a status is a one-line data edit, not a new code branch \u2014 O(1)\r\r\nlookup instead of cascading comparisons.\r\r\n- **The fallback carries the ranges:** `code // 100` recovers the \"hundreds bucket\" that the\r\r\noriginal `code < 300` checks expressed, so the concise version preserves behavior for unlisted codes\r\r\n without re-adding branches.\r\r\n- **Proving equivalence:** identical byte size + `diff` exit 0 + `difflib`/`==` are three\r\r\nindependent confirmations \u2014 behavioral equivalence is shown by evidence, not asserted.\r\r\n\u2500\u2500\u25